# Subagent delegation

Shared context: `AGENTS.md`. Orchestration playbook: skill **`agent-orchestration`**. Quality: `quality-bar.mdc`. Boundaries: `write-boundaries.mdc`.

## Prefer delegation when

| Situation | Subagent |
|-----------|----------|
| New routes / god-file risk / architecture contracts | `architecture-guardian` |
| create-run, runner tools, artifacts, SSE/events | `run-pipeline-engineer` |
| CDE/IS/Git/ZIP, bindings, pack overlays, IS `test/` writes | `source-approach-engineer` |
| Extension MV3, pairing, AST save, storageState | `chrome-recorder-engineer` |
| `database/*.sql`, search_path, bindings DDL | `schema-migration-engineer` |
| Auth, cookies, encryption keys, secrets-resolve | `auth-crypto-guardian` |
| Choosing/running gates, CI-equivalent verify, test placement | `platform-verifier` |

## Skills

| Skill | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `agent-orchestration` | Classify, graph, parallelize, escalate |
| `feature-development` | Cross-module features |
| `bug-fix` | Defects / stuck runs |
| `security-change` | HIGH security work |
| `platform-verify` | Gate ladder |
| `forward-migration` | Forward SQL |
| `pack-overlay` | Pack overlays |

## Parallel vs serialize

- **Parallel:** disjoint file ownership (e.g. extension vs pack-overlay investigations/edits).
- **Serialize:** DDL → code using new columns; any two writers on the same files; `platform-verifier` after implementers.
- **Handoff:** short JSON only (see `agent-orchestration`); never whole chat / whole files.

## Main agent keeps

Orchestration, trivial edits, user communication, merging specialist structured output, human escalation.

## Default verify policy

MEDIUM+: skill `platform-verify` / `platform-verifier`.  
Credentialed `live-check`: only if the user explicitly asks.

## Anti-patterns

- Spawning all subagents for a one-line fix
- Circular handoffs (A→B→A)
- Re-exploring architecture in every specialist
- Inventing Frontend/Backend/DevOps agents that do not exist here
- Claiming done without Verification evidence on MEDIUM+
- Writing outside IS `test/` (`IS_TEST_REL`)
